  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Actions of Social Cohesion for Sustainable Reintegration and Violence Prevention in El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to contribute to the prevention of all forms of violence, in particular domestic violence, that youth, youth at risk of migrating irregularly, and youth returnees face in El Salvador, Guatemala, and Honduras, through participatory, empowerment, and capacity-building initiatives focused on social cohesion, gender-related issues, psychosocial assistance, reintegration, among others. In coordination with relevant stakeholders and local/return communities, IOM will promote the strengthening of community resilience, coexistence of young people, and regulatory frameworks to address and raise-awareness on violence prevention.</narrative>
  </description>
